    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1970-p27.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "If \\(r\\) is the inradius and \\(s\\) the semiperimeter, the triangle’s area is \\(K=rs.\\) Its perimeter is \\(2s.\\) The given equality yields \\[ rs=2s. \\] Since \\(s\\gt0,\\) we obtain \\(r=2.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Express the area in terms of the inradius and semiperimeter",
        "Use \\(K=rs\\) and perimeter \\(=2s\\)"
